<title>NETHERLANDS: Suez cuts NKF to sell from hold.</title>
<headline>Suez cuts NKF to sell from hold.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Feb 11 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>NKF Holding     Cable producer 56.00  Suez Nederland</p>
<p>COMMENT: SELL (from Hold). In the second half of January 1997, the German cable market suffered a dramatic increase in pressure on prices of power cables. The normal price erosion of 5-10 pct surged to approximately 25 pct. This segment concerns some 100 million guilders turnover (17 pct of NKF power cable sales, 7.5 pct of total sales). We estimate this developement to depress results for at least a year. Given current share price we believe shares are overvalued at 11.8 times 1997-earnings.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS		   P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)	6.81		  10.2	2.25</p>
<p>    1997		   4.75		  11.8	1.60</p>
<p>    1998		   5.50		  10.2	2.00</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
